#: src/reference/lints.md:80
msgid ""
"Checks for dependency version requirements that do not explicitly specify a "
"full `major.minor.patch` version requirement, such as `serde = \"1\"` or "
"`serde = \"1.0\"`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:84
msgid ""
"This lint currently only applies to caret requirements (the [default "
"requirements](specifying-dependencies.md#default-requirements))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:89
msgid ""
"Version requirements without an explicit full version can be misleading "
"about the actual minimum supported version. For example, `serde = \"1\"` has "
"an implicit minimum bound of `1.0.0`. If your code actually requires "
"features from `1.0.219`, the implicit minimum bound of `1.0.0` gives a false "
"impression about compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:96
msgid "Specifying the full version helps with:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:98
msgid "Accurate minimum version documentation"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:99
msgid "Better compatibility with `-Z minimal-versions`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:100
msgid "Clearer dependency constraints for consumers"
msgstr ""

